Experiment 1: First Palindromic String in an Array
Aim

To find the first palindromic string in an array of strings and analyse its time complexity.

Algorithm
Start from the first string in the array.
Check whether the string is a palindrome by comparing its first and last characters, then moving inward.
If it is a palindrome, print it and stop.
If not, move to the next string and repeat step 2.
If no string is a palindrome, print “No palindromic string found”.
Pseudo code
isPalindrome(s)
  i = 0, j = length(s) - 1
  while i < j
      if s[i] != s[j]
          return false
      i++, j--
  return true

FirstPalindrome(words, n)
  for i = 0 to n-1
      if isPalindrome(words[i])
          print words[i]
          return
  print "No palindromic string found"
Source code (C)
c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int isPalindrome(char s[]) {
    int i = 0, j = (int)strlen(s) - 1;
    while (i < j) {
        if (s[i] != s[j])
            return 0;
        i++;
        j--;
    }
    return 1;
}

int main() {
    char words[5][20] = {"abc", "car", "ada", "racecar", "hello"};
    int n = 5, i, found = 0;

    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        if (isPalindrome(words[i])) {
            printf("First palindromic string: %s\n", words[i]);
            found = 1;
            break;
        }
    }

    if (found == 0)
        printf("No palindromic string found\n");

    return 0;
}
Output
First palindromic string: ada
Result

The first palindromic string in the array was found as “ada”.

Time complexity: Worst case O(n × m), where n is the number of strings and m is the length of the longest string. Best case O(m), when the first string is a palindrome.
Space complexity: O(1).
